{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
  "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 09-1298, General Dynamics v. United States, and the consolidated case, 09-1302, the Boeing Company v. United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner Argument (Phillips)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under those circumstances, it seems to me that the statement in this Court's decision in United States v. Reynolds, which is that the government is certainly free to assert the state-secrets privilege, but when it does so, it has to assume certain responsibilities that come from it, at least in the circumstances where the United States is the moving party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- why wasn't the need to share that technology a part of this contract or a condition to the contract? I've gone through the contract -- or, not all of it; enough of it. I haven't found anywhere in the contract that it requires the U.S. to share information with you. Does that have anything to do with what due process would require? Meaning -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: The two questions I'd have is, first of all -- Justice Sotomayor, sorry; I did not -- I did have her question, because what that suggests is, in this case, it's not unfair to hold your client in this case. And you just read the two circuit court opinions here, and you think this is a defense coming out of long in the past that doesn't have much substance to it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, the Petitioners as a formal matter were the moving party; isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Phillips",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0001-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "termination carries with it a lot of collateral consequences, it exposes you to subsequent problems in the contracting context, it creates the possibility of debarment in -- in future proceedings"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Phillips."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: Well, for several reasons. One is that is the affirmative use of the Federal courts to alter the legal status quo. I think the principle of Reynolds is that -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I have this -- this question about due process: The components of the due process analysis, it seems to me, are what is reasonable, what's necessary in the case, what's unconscionable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Am I -- am I right that this contract did specify certain information that the government agreed to give the Petitioner?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: I have to say, it is a very odd thing to bid on a highly -- a multi-billion-dollar contract on the assumption that they're going to get some technology that they haven't even specified."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Are you saying it was not impossible to do it at that weight?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: General, do you have the citation to that footnote you referred to in the -- the 605(b)? I can find it later, but -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: It's page 32, and I'd also refer the Court to the court of appeals appendix page 19567, which is the page of the contract itself that incorporates the provision. The provision is FAR 52.233-1(h), and it says that -- it mandates performance and compliance with the contract even when there -- in the contracting officer's decision, even when a decision is under appeal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If that -- if you're right about that, the government's absolute right, could you withhold it from other contracts of these contractors?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Katyal",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KATYAL: That's absolutely right. The -- the Federal rules and the Contract Disputes Act provide us an offset so that we could -- we don't have to actually seek the 1.35 billion from their coffers, as he colorfully called it, \"reaching into\"; we can just offset it against future contracts, and the Federal courts would be out of the business altogether about that 1.35 billion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1585fe0dc7d9-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: It's the \"go away\" principle of our jurisprudence, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1298",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "1585fe0dc7d9ec2398cd84ee26dd0bd26b224290ffd3ea012d9346f59b9d2d83",
